 text=f'''# Six-model E1/E2 study: verified partial completion and scientific blocker\n\n**MobileSkinXAI: An Explainable Cross-Dataset Lightweight Deep Learning Framework for Mobile-Based Skin Cancer Screening.**\n\nStatus: BLOCKED_BY_PREDECLARED_TEACHER_QUALIFICATION. This is not a new controller failure. M1 recovered without retraining; M2 and M4 completed exactly once with repaired early stopping; M3 E2 and all six E1 checkpoints unchanged.\n\n{table(rows)}\n\n## Qualification failure\n\nThe immutable00_Protocol/LOCKED_PROTOCOL.md (paragraph13) and CONFIGURATIONS.json require joint M4's best PAD validation declared-lesion macro-F1 to be strictly greater than joint M3's best, margin0. The final teacher score is **{q['teacher_validation_F1']:.12f}**, compared with **{q['student_validation_F1']:.12f}**. Difference: **{100*(q['teacher_validation_F1']-q['student_validation_F1']):+.4f} percentage points**. Thus qualification is false. The controller stopped before any M5/M5-LR optimization. No replacement teacher, altered gate, extra trial, continuation, learning-rate change or substitute method was used.\n\nTeacher selected checkpoint: `{q['teacher_checkpoint']}`\nTeacher SHA256: `{q['teacher_sha256']}`\nFrozen M3 parent: `{q['student_checkpoint']}`\nStudent SHA256: `{q['student_sha256']}`\n\n## Controller correction and M1 recovery\n\nAll11deterministic tests passed before GPU training, including an actual CPU AdamW stagnation loop and M1 history replay. The original engine remains sealed and unchanged. Versioned engine_fixed_v1.py adds the in-loop stop check and explicit stopping metadata while preserving all training-method functions. M2 and M4 committed exactly their prescribed stopping epochs with no subsequent epoch artifacts. Their best/last states contain model, finite optimizer states and complete Torch/CUDA/Python/NumPy RNG state. Scheduler/scaler states are inapplicable to the fixed-LR BF16 implementation.\n\nM1 selected epoch10 was reconstructed solely from epochs1–16; all23committed epoch checkpoints and partial epoch24 files remain. Prescribed stopped-run duration483.097325s is separate from actual committed consumption731.330802s; unknown partial epoch24 overhead is additional. The corrected completion manifest explicitly documents this deviation rather than rewriting history or last.pt. No M1 optimization occurred during recovery.\n\n## Integrity audit\n\n'''+ '\n'.join('- PASS: '+s for s in checks)+'''\n\n## Unfinished deliverables and next protocol decision\n\nM5 and M5-LR are scientifically blocked under the current locked protocol. All-six final evaluation, comparison tables, new Grad-CAM and publication figures were deliberately not run: the user requires all six E2 checkpoints to be verified and frozen before these operations. No complete six-model results or figure index is fabricated. Existing M3 E1/E2 results and previous figure packages remain valid and unchanged.\n\nContinuing the enhanced comparison requires an explicit scientifically justified protocol amendment addressing failed teacher qualification. It would be inappropriate to silently waive the criterion, retrain M4 until it passes, pick a teacher from test performance, or relabel ordinary supervised MobileNetV4 training as the enhanced method. There is no automatic further training or evaluation.\n\nPAD remains POST-HOC EXPLORATORY. Seven test melanoma declaredlesions and single-seed training limit inference. E1 is zero-shot source-only transfer; E2 has labeled target exposure and is supervised joint-domain learning. The comparison of historical E1 and E2 recipes is confounded by selection/augmentation/weighting/budget differences, so no isolated causal, novel-algorithm, clinical-safety or independent-external superiority claim is supported. Flutter and TFLite were not modified/exported.\n\n## Evidence paths\n\n13_Reports/M1_RECOVERY_REPORT.md\n13_Reports/TRAINING_CONTROLLER_FIX_REPORT.md\n13_Reports/CONTROLLER_TEST_RESULTS.json\n13_Reports/FINAL_E2_TRAINING_STATUS.md\n13_Reports/training_console_fixed_v1.log\n00_Protocol/TEACHER_QUALIFICATION.json\n03_E2_Training/M1, M2 and M4: histories, commits, selected/last checkpoint states and completion manifests.\n'''
